# Plain labels

Criterion 2 (consistent terminology) applies to the thesis body only.

On a diagram, a slide, or in chat: if a line would need a translation, rewrite
the line. Name the people or the program, then say what it does.

Do not mint a hyphenated substitute (`same-design pair` for `matched pair`).
Do not keep `runtime`, `framework`, `matched pair`, `stateless transformation`,
or `stores no state` on a figure when a plain sentence exists.

A label the author has to ask about has failed.
